//? Title: Cohen–Sutherland: Outcodes, Half-Planes and Real Decisions
//? Subtitle: The original four segments, an inconclusive-mask counterexample and checked native intersections
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A renderer needs the portion of a directed line segment that lies in a closed
rectangular viewport, or a decision that nothing is visible. Testing every
boundary intersection wastes work when a segment is already inside or wholly
outside one side. Cohen–Sutherland uses four-bit endpoint codes to resolve
those cases first. We retain the original four segments, inspect actual native
edge decisions and show a zero-AND pair that still misses the viewport. A
complete small grid measures trivial and intersection paths. The checked core
validates all inputs, retains closed-boundary contacts and uses widened
supporting-line arithmetic; this remains floating geometry, not an exact predicate.
)

\toc

> Nine regions and two decisive bit tests

Let the viewport be [xmin,xmax]×[ymin,ymax], with inclusive, ordered finite
bounds. Give a point bit 1 when x<xmin, bit 2 when x>xmax, bit 4 when y<ymin
and bit 8 when y>ymax. Equality is inside that half-plane. Combining these
tests divides the plane into nine regions; opposite horizontal bits cannot
both occur for an ordered rectangle, and neither can opposite vertical bits.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cohen_outcodes.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(28,950);
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke grid;grid.color={148,163,184};grid.dashed=true;
  d.polygon({{0,0},{10,0},{10,10},{0,10}},{219,234,254});
  for(double edge:{0.,10.}) {
    d.path({{edge,-9},{edge,19}},grid);d.path({{-9,edge},{19,edge}},grid);
  }
  std::print("| region centre x | region centre y | actual four-bit outcode |\n| ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(double y:{15.,5.,-5.})for(double x:{-5.,5.,15.}) {
    const auto mask=dm::algorithms::cohen_sutherland_outcode(x,y,0,0,10,10);
    const auto bits=std::format("{:04b}",unsigned(mask));
    d.text({x,y},bits,25);
    std::print("| {:.0f} | {:.0f} | {} |\n",x,y,bits);
  }
  d.text({5,22},"Closed viewport: boundary equality belongs inside",23)
   .text({5,-12},"left 0001; right 0010; bottom 0100; top 1000",21)
   .save_svg("build/cohen_outcodes.svg");
}
```
