\caption(The native point classifier supplies every region label. The centre is the closed viewport, and corner regions combine one horizontal with one vertical bit.)
\alttext(A square viewport has code 0000. Above, below, left and right have codes 1000, 0100, 0001 and 0010. Corner regions combine their neighbouring outside bits.)

Write c0,c1 for the current endpoint codes. If (c0 OR c1)=0, both points are
inside. A rectangle is convex, so every point between them is inside too:
accept the current segment. If (c0 AND c1)≠0, both points violate the same
closed half-plane. Every convex combination still violates it: reject.
These mask tests avoid intersection arithmetic, but obtaining the codes still
requires coordinate comparisons. A zero AND with nonzero OR is inconclusive.

> The original four segments, with executed edge work

Use the original viewport [0,10]×[0,10] and the same directed inputs. The
historical label “partly in” describes an oblique crossing: both of its original
endpoints are outside. It enters at y=0 and leaves at y=10. In p(t)=(2,−3)+t(6,16),
those parameters are 3/16 and 13/16, yielding (3.125,0) and (6.875,10).

The trace shares the executing kernel with cohen_sutherland_clip(). It records
current endpoints/codes, the selected outside endpoint, the actual intersection
and its new code. The first outside endpoint is chosen, with edge priority
top, bottom, right, left. Each run ends with a separate accept or reject decision.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cohen_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  struct Segment {double x0,y0,x1,y1;std::string_view name;dm::graphics::RGB colour;};
  const std::vector<Segment> input{{-5,5,15,5,"through",{37,99,235}},
    {2,-3,8,13,"partly in",{13,148,136}},{3,3,7,6,"inside",{234,88,12}},
    {-5,20,15,20,"outside",{220,38,38}}};
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(34,1000);
  d.polygon({{0,0},{10,0},{10,10},{0,10}},{241,245,249});
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke original;original.color={148,163,184};original.width=2;
  std::print("| original name | visible | native clipped endpoints | edge cuts | decisions | outcode evaluations |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto& s:input) {
    const auto t=dm::algorithms::cohen_sutherland_clip_trace(s.x0,s.y0,s.x1,s.y1,0,0,10,10);
    const auto& c=t.result;
    d.path({{s.x0,s.y0},{s.x1,s.y1}},original);
    if(c.visible) {
      dm::graphics::DiagramStroke kept;kept.color=s.colour;kept.width=4;
      d.path({{c.x0,c.y0},{c.x1,c.y1}},kept);
      d.ellipse({c.x0,c.y0},.13,.13,s.colour).ellipse({c.x1,c.y1},.13,.13,s.colour);
    }
    const auto ends=c.visible?std::format("({:.3f},{:.3f}) to ({:.3f},{:.3f})",c.x0,c.y0,c.x1,c.y1):"rejected";
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",s.name,c.visible,ends,t.intersections,t.steps.size(),t.outcode_evaluations);
  }
  d.text({5,24},"Original segments and their actual visible fragments",23)
   .text({5,21},"outside: both above",19)
   .text({-2,4},"through",19,{37,99,235})
   .text({11,13},"partly in",19,{13,148,136})
   .text({7,2},"inside",19,{234,88,12})
   .text({5,-7},"Light originals; coloured accepted fragments; equal coordinate scales",18)
   .save_svg("build/cohen_original.svg");
}
```
