| :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| through | true | (0.000,5.000) to (10.000,5.000) | 2 | 3 | 4 |
| partly in | true | (3.125,0.000) to (6.875,10.000) | 2 | 3 | 4 |
| inside | true | (3.000,3.000) to (7.000,6.000) | 0 | 1 | 2 |
| outside | false | rejected | 0 | 1 | 2 |
\image(figures/cohen_original.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The original horizontal and oblique crossings each need two cuts. Inside and shared-above inputs need none. Marked endpoints and equal diagram scales retain the actual geometry.)
\alttext(A square viewport contains a blue horizontal fragment from zero-five to ten-five, a teal oblique fragment from 3.125-zero to 6.875-ten and an orange unchanged interior line. A grey line above the viewport is rejected.)

For a horizontal clipping boundary y=h, solve the supporting-line equation
for x. Rather than recomputing from rounded replacement endpoints, the checked
kernel retains the original coordinates. Its widened numerator is

\[
x(h)=\frac{x_0y_1-x_1y_0+h(x_1-x_0)}{y_1-y_0}.
\]
\alttext(The x coordinate at height h equals x-zero times y-one minus x-one times y-zero plus h times the x difference, divided by the y difference.)

For x=v, interchange x and y. The denominator cannot be zero in a selected
crossing: one current endpoint violates that half-plane while the other
satisfies it, because otherwise the AND test would already reject. The edge
coordinate is pinned to the exact stored boundary. Keeping its small boundary
term separate avoids losing it inside a huge endpoint-minus-boundary expression.
Using the original supporting line also prevents successive rounded cuts from
tilting a line that should touch a corner.

The implementation widens before subtraction and checks working differences
and ratios. If determinant products are unrepresentable, it falls back to
bounded std::lerp interpolation. Free coordinates are projected onto the current
endpoint coordinate range to retain already satisfied half-planes; this is
rounding containment, not an exact-predicate construction. Conversion to the
legacy double result happens only after acceptance.

> Zero AND can miss, and an endpoint can gain a different bit

In the unit viewport, p0=(−1,0.5) has code 0001 and p1=(0.5,2) has code 1000.
Their AND is zero, but the entire line segment misses above the upper-left
corner. Cutting p0 at x=0 gives parameter 2/3 and point (0,1.5). The old left
bit disappears and a new top bit appears. Both remaining endpoints are above,
so the next decision rejects. Counting removed endpoint bits is therefore an
insufficient termination argument.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cohen_inconclusive.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::cohen_sutherland_clip_trace(-1,.5,.5,2,0,0,1,1);
  if(t.result.visible || t.intersections!=1 || t.steps[0].new_code!=8)return 1;
  const std::array<std::string_view,6> names{"accept","reject","top","bottom","right","left"};
  std::print("| decision | code 0 | code 1 | action | replacement code |\n| ---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.steps.size();++i) {
    const auto& s=t.steps[i];
    std::print("| {} | {:04b} | {:04b} | {} | {} |\n",i+1,unsigned(s.code0),unsigned(s.code1),names[static_cast<std::size_t>(s.action)],s.replaced_endpoint<2?std::format("{:04b}",unsigned(s.new_code)):"terminal");
  }
  const auto& cut=t.steps[0];
  std::print("\nActual left-edge intersection ({},{}); visible={}.\n",cut.intersection_x,cut.intersection_y,t.result.visible);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(210,1000);
  d.polygon({{0,0},{1,0},{1,1},{0,1}},{219,234,254});
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke faint;faint.color={148,163,184};faint.width=2;
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke remaining;remaining.color={220,38,38};remaining.width=4;
  d.path({{-1,.5},{.5,2}},faint)
   .path({{double(cut.intersection_x),double(cut.intersection_y)},{.5,2}},remaining)
   .ellipse({double(cut.intersection_x),double(cut.intersection_y)},.025,.025,{220,38,38})
   .text({.15,2.9},"Zero AND leaves an inconclusive case",23)
   .text({-1.05,.3},"p0: 0001",19)
   .text({.85,2.18},"p1: 1000",19)
   .text({-.65,1.7},"cut (0,1.5)\nnew code 1000",18,{220,38,38})
   .text({.5,.45},"closed\nviewport",19)
   .text({.15,-.55},"Both remaining points are above: reject",21)
   .save_svg("build/cohen_inconclusive.svg");
}
```
